{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>I resemble</b> — לקאת — both construct and non-construct also [has] a tav, only the qof when non-construct has a kamatz." "<b>Like the owl</b> — like: את הכוס ואת השלך, and behold, his soul is astounded within it, like the owl that dwells in ruins."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 102, :notes {0 "He observes that the pronominal suffix form לקאת (with tav) occurs in both construct and absolute states; the qoph takes a kamatz only in the absolute (non-construct) form."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:37:46.455152749Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}